🪄
"MagicWords"/en
=== start
¶Say a color or a feeling out loud and the stage obeys your words.¶

¶The magic words. Everything below reads them from this one list, so the words
the stage listens for and the words it asks you for can never disagree.¶
spells: ['red' 'blue' 'green' 'happy' 'sad' 'sleepy' 'spin']

¶We give the places in that list names, to make the spells easier to read.¶
red: 1
blue: 2
green: 3
happy: 4
sad: 5
sleepy: 6
spin: 7

¶Only the last three words count, so each new spell replaces the last, and
lowercasing means Red and red are the same spell.¶
heard: Speech(limit: 3).🔡()

¶Whether a spell was among the last three words said. We look for the spell with
a space on each side, so saying spread doesn't count as saying red, and so a
spell can be more than one word — blue is two words in Vietnamese.¶
ƒ said(which•#)•? (' ' + heard + ' ').has(' ' + spells[which] + ' ')

sky: said(red) ? Color.red
	said(blue) ? Color.blue
		said(green) ? Color.green
			Color.white

mood: said(happy) ? "😄"
	said(sad) ? "😢"
		said(sleepy) ? "😴"
			"😐"

Stage(
	[
		Group(
			Stack('|' 1m)
			[
				Phrase(mood 8m resting: said(spin) ? Sequence.spin() ø)
				Phrase(heard = '' ? 'say: ' + spells.join(', ') heard 0.75m)
			]
		)
	]
	background: sky
)
